WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.680
Octopus drummers, snazzy outfits,&nbsp;
and the one reason you don't wanna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:09.240
be the seventh Batman — keep watching for&nbsp;
the low-down on Jason Momoa's Aquaman.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.340
Before Aquaman came along, Jason Momoa was best&nbsp;
known for playing the role of the barbarian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:19.560
warlord Khal Drogo in Game of Thrones —&nbsp;
as well a less-than-stellar turn as Conan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:24.600
the Barbarian in a critically derided reboot&nbsp;
of that franchise. Basically, the actor had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:29.820
made a name for himself playing rough, uncouth&nbsp;
anti-heroes, rather than kingly superheroes.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.720
When Momoa first got the call from&nbsp;
Warner to audition for the DCEU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.440
he did not imagine for a second that he&nbsp;
was being offered the role of Aquaman.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.420
""I'm like, 'I'm just going to basically be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:43.920
bad guy. I'm going to fight Batman and&nbsp;
Superman. I'm gonna play the villain.'"

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.900
But Momoa was soon informed by director Zack&nbsp;
Snyder that he would instead be auditioning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.740
to play Aquaman. The actor had a hard&nbsp;
time imagining himself as the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:57.420
from the comics. However, Snyder, who was&nbsp;
a huge fan of Momoa's turn as Khal Drogo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.620
assured the actor that he would be the right&nbsp;
choice to bring Aquaman to the big screen.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:07.200
On the surface, there seems to be little in&nbsp;
common between Jason Momoa and Aquaman. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.940
character in the comics is very blond and very&nbsp;
white, and, in his initial on screen appearances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.960
totally lighthearted. He's more of a&nbsp;
holdover from the Golden Age of comics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.340
than someone who encapsulates the warrior&nbsp;
physique and brooding presence of Momoa.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:24.840
But the actor found he had more in common&nbsp;
with Arthur Curry than previously suspected.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:28.740
Momoa is of Native Hawaiian descent,&nbsp;
and aquatic activities were a part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:33.120
of the actor's life long before Aquaman&nbsp;
came calling. In fact, he even has some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.500
real-life experience with a classic Aquaman&nbsp;
trick. When he was asked whether he has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.000
practicing telepathy with sea creatures,&nbsp;
Momoa told a crowd at Walker Stalker Con:

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.660
"No, but I've rode some dolphins&nbsp;
before, so I can pull on that."

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:50.940
Additionally, Momoa has revealed that he had been&nbsp;
studying to become a marine biologist before he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:55.380
decided to take a chance on becoming an actor.&nbsp;
But the greatest thing about playing Aquaman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.380 --> 00:02:00.900
for Momoa was that it allowed him to pay tribute&nbsp;
to Polynesian gods. He told Walker Stalker Con:

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:04.620
"Our gods, Kahoali, Maui, all these water gods.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.980
It's really cool and an honor to&nbsp;
be playing a [water] character."

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:13.320
Despite enjoying a positive reception after&nbsp;
his initial cameo in Batman v Superman:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:18.480
Dawn of Justice and his larger role in Justice&nbsp;
League, Aquaman still had to prove himself with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.340
a solo movie. Luckily, Momoa had the help&nbsp;
of perennial hitmaker James Wan, who was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:28.380
able to craft Aquaman into a blockbuster movie&nbsp;
that fans and critics alike could get behind.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:32.940
Aquaman was a major departure for Wan, who&nbsp;
was better known for his horror movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:36.540
and he chose the character because&nbsp;
Aquaman was relatively unknown to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:40.500
mainstream film audiences at the&nbsp;
time. He told Business Insider:

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:44.820
"[The studio] asked me which superhero I&nbsp;
would be interested in. I picked Aquaman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:48.540
because it's the one everyone makes fun of,&nbsp;
so there wouldn't be a lot of pressure."

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:52.920
Free of the burden of expectations,&nbsp;
Wan was able to craft his own unique&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:56.220
take on the superhero genre.&nbsp;
He explained to Vital Thrills:

00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:01.080
"My template wasn't other superhero films.&nbsp;
My template was more like traditional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:06.420
adventure-fantasy films or coming-of-age stories,&nbsp;
rite of passage and all of that kind of stuff."

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:12.120
Inspired by fantasy films from the '80s, Wan was&nbsp;
able to chart a radical narrative for Aquaman's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:17.280
big-screen debut that feels excitingly different&nbsp;
yet comfortingly familiar at the same time.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:21.780
If you were to ask most actors&nbsp;
about their dream DC superhero role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.840
chances are you're going to hear&nbsp;
the word "Batman." Certainly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:29.460
few actors would choose Aquaman, who had&nbsp;
long been seen as a walking punchline.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:30.960
"I've got friends coming over tonight!"

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:34.380
"These lobsters walked right up&nbsp;
to the door — anyone hungry?"

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:38.580
But Jason Momoa always knew he had the&nbsp;
opportunity to do something special with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:42.660
the character. The actor told The Independent&nbsp;
that, when he was hired to play Arthur Curry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.320
he was given the freedom to interpret the&nbsp;
character in a new way "from the ground&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:51.720
up." According to Momoa, he was chosen for the&nbsp;
role due to certain personal attributes that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:56.100
he could transfer to the character, helping to&nbsp;
bring Aquaman to life in a compelling manner.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.420
When it was time to make his solo movie,&nbsp;
James Wan also encouraged Momoa to continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:04.260
to interpret the character in his own&nbsp;
way. With so much creative freedom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:09.600
maybe it's not surprising that Momoa would prefer&nbsp;
to be Aquaman than yet another Batman. He said:

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.180
"It's nice not being the seventh Batman. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:15.000
nice to be the first one. And&nbsp;
good luck being the next one."

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:20.400
During many superhero debuts, lead actors&nbsp;
face the uphill task of making audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:24.720
care about an unknown character. But when&nbsp;
Jason Momoa signed on to play Aquaman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.680
he had an even more difficult task:&nbsp;
making the public like a superhero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.040
who had been actively mocked and&nbsp;
treated as a joke for decades.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.940
Of course, Zack Snyder and Warner took&nbsp;
the right step by casting an actor who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:39.600
could look badass doing literally&nbsp;
anything. Momoa was very aware that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:42.840
he needed to reinvent Aquaman as&nbsp;
a commanding and imposing figure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:48.360
which is why he had a strong dislike for a line&nbsp;
in Joss Whedon's 2017 version of Justice League.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:50.160
"I hear you can talk to fish."

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.500
Momoa later told EW:

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.840
"I'm like, 'Don't put this line in there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:58.800
because that's all people are going to talk&nbsp;
about. Do you want me to make him cool or not?"

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.380
Fortunately, that one-off joke was not enough to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:04.200
detract from the energy that&nbsp;
Momoa brought to the role.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:08.820
Iconic comic book heroes often have&nbsp;
iconic origins, and filmmakers change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:13.080
those stories at their peril. Aquaman's&nbsp;
origin story is less well-known, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:18.540
and filmmaker James Wan made plenty of&nbsp;
changes to it while making his 2018 movie.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:22.440
The most obvious difference is that&nbsp;
Aquaman in the comics is blonde-haired,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:27.060
blue-eyed, and pale, whereas Jason&nbsp;
Momoa is of Polynesian descent;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:31.320
his version of Arthur Curry is shown to be&nbsp;
of mixed race. Then there's the fact that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:37.140
in the comics, Aquaman is usually depicted as a&nbsp;
very serious character who is acutely conscious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:40.980
of his royal heritage, and his manner&nbsp;
of speaking reflects his noble birth.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:46.620
But in the movie, Arthur is closer to Momoa's&nbsp;
real-life personality, a fun-loving dudebro-type&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:52.380
who drinks beer in bars and doesn't take himself&nbsp;
too seriously. The details of Aquaman's journey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:56.640
to becoming the King of Atlantis also turn out&nbsp;
much differently than they do in the comics.

00:05:57.180 --> 00:06:02.340
2018's Aquaman is sometimes described as a&nbsp;
little over-the-top, and the biggest example&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:06.360
of this excess is generally considered to&nbsp;
be the fight scene between Arthur and Orm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:10.020
in which, among other things, an&nbsp;
octopus can be seen playing the drums.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:13.320
The octopus drummer might seem like&nbsp;
a bizarre addition to the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:17.580
but there are actually a couple of solid&nbsp;
reasons for its presence. First of all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:22.920
the octopus in the film is inspired by Topo,&nbsp;
Aquaman's long-time octopus ally in the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:27.420
who played a variety of musical instruments.&nbsp;
James Wan told The Huffington Post:

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:32.340
"So I'm like, 'OK, how do I take that and&nbsp;
bring it into my movie and make it cool?'"

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:36.240
Additionally, Wan saw a drum-playing&nbsp;
octopus placed in the middle of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:40.560
action as essentially fulfilling the same&nbsp;
role as the war-rig guitarist from Mad Max:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:42.840
Fury Road. He explained to the Metro:

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:46.620
"In that movie there is literally&nbsp;
a guitar guy having flames shooting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:51.360
from his instrument. It doesn't do anything&nbsp;
for the narrative. But it creates a really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:55.080
unique world. That was my goal for&nbsp;
[the drum-playing octopus] as well."

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:58.320
"Oh, what a day! What a lovely day!"

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:03.000
One of the things that makes Aquaman better&nbsp;
than the average superhero movie is that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:07.500
does not wholly revolve around Arthur Curry,&nbsp;
but is instead filled with other interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:12.060
characters who make a real impact on the plot.&nbsp;
Two such characters are Arthur's parents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:16.620
whose relationship with each other and Arthur&nbsp;
powers the central narrative of the film.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:20.940
The role of Arthur's father, Tom, is&nbsp;
played by veteran actor Temuera Morrison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:24.660
who credits Jason Momoa with&nbsp;
getting him the part. Apparently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:29.760
Momoa had been inspired by Morrison's role in&nbsp;
Once Were Warriors. Morrison told Now To Love:

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:34.080
"Jason saw Once Were Warriors when he&nbsp;
was growing up in Iowa, and because his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:38.160
father's Hawaiian, it really impinged on&nbsp;
his cultural consciousness and identity."

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:42.420
Meanwhile, Nicole Kidman agreed to&nbsp;
play Queen Atlanna in Aquaman mainly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:45.900
due to her desire to work with&nbsp;
the film's director. She told EW:

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:49.980
"[James Wan is] a really good friend of&nbsp;
mine, and he offered to let me play Queen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:54.060
Atlanna. As soon as he said I could wear&nbsp;
mother-of-pearl and be a mermaid warrior,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:58.680
I said I'm done. Please. If there is one thing&nbsp;
I have to do in my life, I have to be that."

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:01.260
The actress saw the role as an opportunity to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:04.560
"have some fun" while working with a&nbsp;
director whom she had long admired.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:09.120
The character of Aquaman went through a few&nbsp;
changes from his classic look while making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:13.740
the jump to live-action film. But the truth&nbsp;
is that Aquaman includes three distinctly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:18.480
famous looks for Arthur Curry from the comics by&nbsp;
featuring them on members of his extended family.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:24.000
First up is Arthur himself. His look closely&nbsp;
resembles the Aquaman from the comics in the '90s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:28.200
when the character had long locks, body&nbsp;
armor resembling the tattoos from the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:32.880
and a disinclination to wear a shirt. Then&nbsp;
there is the classic, bright blonde-haired,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:37.260
clean-shaven look for Aquaman from the&nbsp;
comics, which, in the movie, was given to Orm.

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:41.280
Finally, there's the suit given to&nbsp;
Arthur and Orm's ancestor, King Atlan:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:45.540
the classic green and gold colors of the&nbsp;
Aquaman suit from the comics combined with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:49.860
a royal cloak and a crown. This look&nbsp;
closely resembles a much older Arthur&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:54.420
Curry's uniform in Alex Ross and Mark Waid's&nbsp;
classic graphic novel series Kingdom Come.

00:08:55.080 --> 00:09:00.120
While Arthur Curry and his half-brother, Orm,&nbsp;
are the center of the story in Aquaman, fans also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:05.340
responded well to the supporting villain, Black&nbsp;
Manta, who is played by Yahya Abdul-Mateen II.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:10.320
After Arthur allows Manta's father to die early&nbsp;
in the movie, the latter is overcome with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:14.880
desire for revenge, and his journey towards&nbsp;
vengeance makes for a compelling subplot.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:18.900
"Kill him and the woman he's&nbsp;
with and you will be rewarded."

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:20.700
"Killing him is my reward."

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.420
In the comics, Black Manta is one&nbsp;
of Aquaman's most famous enemies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:29.520
but he almost didn't make the cut when the studio&nbsp;
was preparing Aquaman for his first live-action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:34.620
movie. It was the combined efforts of director&nbsp;
James Wan and producer Geoff Johns that kept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:39.960
Black Manta in the script — and looking just like&nbsp;
he does in the comics. Johns told Geeks of Color:

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:44.460
"There was a moment when the script was really&nbsp;
going and James texted me or emailed me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:49.140
and said Black Manta's story may be too big&nbsp;
for this movie. [...] And I didn't reply,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:54.960
I just went to his office and I said, 'Black Manta&nbsp;
has to be in the movie.' He was like, 'I know!'"

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:58.080
Fortunately, Manta did become a part of Aquaman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:01.320
and he is expected to appear&nbsp;
in the upcoming sequel, too.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:07.380
A few eyebrows were raised when Jason Momoa&nbsp;
was first cast as Aquaman in the DCEU. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:10.620
actor proved all the naysayers&nbsp;
wrong, however, when he became a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:15.240
huge fan-favorite and helped score the solo&nbsp;
Aquaman movie a billion-dollar gross at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:19.740
box office. And now the actor is ready to kick&nbsp;
his involvement with the franchise up a notch.

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:24.420
In 2021, while discussing Aquaman and the&nbsp;
Lost Kingdom on The Drew Barrymore Show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:27.840
Momoa revealed that he felt so&nbsp;
strongly about the direction the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:31.920
superhero franchise should take that he&nbsp;
came up with a treatment for the sequel.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:35.280
"We did the first treatment, and then&nbsp;
James and our original writer, David,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.640
finished it off, and all of our hearts are in it."

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:42.180
The actor also revealed that he felt&nbsp;
much more involved in the project as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:45.780
a writing partner than he would have if&nbsp;
he had simply been following a script.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:49.560
And however The Lost Kingdom turns&nbsp;
out, one thing seems to be certain:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:53.580
Jason Momoa is going to be sticking&nbsp;
with Aquaman for a long time to come.

